<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαυχενίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut off by the neck,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				34.2.22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦρον ἀ.</span>
			<i>tame</i> a bull <i>by forcing back his neck,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Her.</u>
				12b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
			</span></i> Jun.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Im.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>shake off</i> the yoke <i>from the neck, get free by
				struggling,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.34
			</span></i> O., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.305
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
